From: EmberBSD contributors
Subject: [PATCH] imagination: reserve all sampler words in the IDFWDF ABI

Mesa 26.2.4 copies four sampler dwords at offset 4. Reserve these words
before the two address dwords. The old seven-dword allocation overflowed
by one dword and the address overwrote two sampler words.

The common header is shared with common.cl. Regenerate the USC library
with this header; do not combine old shaders with the new host layout.
MIT; original Imagination Technologies attribution remains in the files.
AI-assisted downstream fix. Not submitted to or accepted by upstream.

--- a/src/imagination/common/pvr_iface.h
+++ b/src/imagination/common/pvr_iface.h
@@ -117,7 +117,8 @@ enum pvr_idfwdf_sr_data {
    PVR_IDFWDF_DATA_TEX = 0,
    PVR_IDFWDF_DATA_SMP = 4,
 
-   PVR_IDFWDF_DATA_ADDR_LO,
+   /* The sampler occupies four shared-register dwords. */
+   PVR_IDFWDF_DATA_ADDR_LO = 8,
    PVR_IDFWDF_DATA_ADDR_HI,
 
    _PVR_IDFWDF_DATA_COUNT,
